cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Universal Right-Triangle Reflection Sequence (Unequal Legs)"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vico
    family-names: Bonfioli
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    email: vicobonfioli@gmail.com
abstract: >
  For every right triangle in the plane with positive unequal rational
  legs, the BFS orbit-growth sequence of its three side-reflections
  agrees with one common sequence u_d (OEIS A396406) through depth 32,
  and this is sharp: the (1,2) triangle deviates at depth 33. The
  natural all-depths universality conjecture is refuted: for every
  rational, indeed every algebraic, shape an explicit nontrivial kernel
  element (a conjugated product of glide-reflection squares) forces a
  first deviation at depth n_T between max(33, c_T) and 24 c_T + 8. The
  common sequence is exactly the orbit growth of the generic right
  triangle (transcendental leg ratio), whose group is virtually the
  lamplighter Z wr Z; its translation lattice 2(t-1)Z[t] and the kernel
  of every algebraic specialization are computed exactly, and the word
  metric is given by a closed form whose upper bound is proved and whose
  lower bound is stated as a conjecture, verified with 0 exceptions on
  all 275823 elements to depth 24. In n dimensions the right-angled
  Coxeter envelope of the orthoscheme has rational growth with rate
  r_n = 1 + 2 cos(2 pi / (n+3)); for n >= 3 every kernel element of word
  length 6 lies in a rank-two standard parabolic, and the rank-two
  relations are classified by rank-0 descent on the elliptic curves
  24a1, 72a2 and y^2 = x^3 - x. These give the collision depth
  unconditionally on two of the three strata. On the third, the depth is
  infinite exactly when the affine representation is injective, which is
  open for n >= 3; an earlier claim of unconditional faithfulness from
  det Q_n = -prod a_i^2 was a non sequitur and is withdrawn. On the
  arithmetic of the growth series, the Polya-Carlson dichotomy for the
  four catalytic blocks is unconditional, and the rational branch is
  excluded unconditionally for the two denominators, leaving the two
  numerators under an unproved coefficient-growth hypothesis. The travel
  resolvent is transcendental over Q(x) unconditionally. The relaxed
  companion V and the true series U = A396406 are transcendental over
  Q(x) conditionally: V on a junction non-vanishing hypothesis, U on
  that and on the invariance of the travel block, both on a transfer
  model. The growth rate is beta_2 = 1.4916177871..., which excludes
  3/2.
keywords:
  - right-triangle reflection group
  - Coxeter groups
  - orbit growth
  - lamplighter group
  - wreath product
  - cyclic ideal
  - Fibonacci sequence
  - orthoscheme
  - Mordell descent
  - faithfulness
  - transcendence
  - q-series
  - natural boundary
